quotes":[{"c":"SM 2019 Q3","e":"sm","d":"2019-11-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jay Ottoson","x":"I just wanted to take a minute ahead of Q&A here just to emphasize our recent progress on cost reduction, because I think we've under-solved to some extent a noteworthy achievement.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/sm-energy-co-sm-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"SM 2019 Q3","e":"sm","d":"2019-11-01","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Herb Vogel","x":"But we see a clear path to additional cost savings and productivity improvements and that we anticipate enhancing returns where the wells will be competitive in the portfolio and that will be even more so, once those midstream contracts expire or have lower rates as we've talked about before.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/01/sm-energy-co-sm-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"SM 2020 Q2","e":"sm","d":"2020-07-31","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Wade Pursell","x":"We have lowered guidance for LOE for the year to reflect cost savings but do expect third- and fourth-quarter operating expenses to be higher than the second quarter on a per-BOE basis, inclusive of workovers.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/01/sm-energy-sm-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcript.aspx"},{"c":"SM 2020 Q3","e":"sm","d":"2020-10-30","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Gail Nicholson","x":"Looking at LOE, you guys lowered the full-year guide.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/10/31/sm-energy-sm-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"SM 2020 Q4","e":"sm","d":"2021-02-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Karl Blunden","x":"As you think about what the optimal capital structure is going forward, I'd be interested in your thoughts, and maybe this is more for Wade, on the benefit of interest cost savings from adding second lien debt relative to the increased flexibility you have from issuing regular way, high-yield bonds.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/18/sm-energy-sm-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"SM 2021 Q1","e":"sm","d":"2021-04-30","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Herb Vogel","x":"But, no, it's -- we're just looking at it, but we maintain guidance for the year and 2022 looks the same.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/30/sm-energy-sm-q1-2021-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"SM 2026 Q1","e":"sm","d":"2026-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Elizabeth McDonald","x":"Faster cycle times, strong well performance and synergy-driven cost savings are enabling our teams to do more with less.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/sm-energy-sm-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"SM 2026 Q1","e":"sm","d":"2026-05-07","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Zachary Parham","x":"You're in a bit of a unique situation in that you closed a merger in 1Q and you had plans in place to allow some acquired volumes to fall to kind of rightsize that asset.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/06/01/sm-energy-sm-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"SM 2026 Q3","e":"sm","d":"2026-11-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Blake Mckenna","x":"So you're going to have higher effort to smaller items, and that's just a natural part of chasing cost savings down.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/04/sm-energy-sm-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[35,1,2595,0,0,0,2010,327],[36,1,3409,0,0,0,1988,1014],[37,1,2132,0,0,0,1327,537],[38,1,3471,0,0,0,2304,771],[39,1,5808,0,0,0,3601,1687],[40,1,2386,0,0,0,1524,507],[42,1,7142,0,0,0,5153,1144],[43,1,3382,0,0,0,2204,875],[44,1,7135,0,0,0,5344,1399],[45,1,3373,0,0,0,2005,1109],[47,1,3861,0,0,0,2277,1266],[49,1,5582,0,0,0,4015,954],[50,1,2690,0,0,0,1872,567],[63,1,5643,0,0,0,3891,1328],[64,1,4514,0,0,0,3115,1171],[65,1,5079,0,0,0,3789,1023],[67,1,5479,0,0,0,2575,260